# This repository as a fixture for its own gates.
#
# Added because one fixture was not enough. dora-loop has no gates/ directory,
# so the docs gate's structural sections -- gate documented, fault named in
# prose, exit-code table, proof-count drift -- never executed against it. It
# checks far fewer claims there than here. A coverage analysis deleted all four
# sections and the corpus stayed green.
#
# n/a is a declaration, not an omission. There is no JVM build here, so the two
# JVM gates must return exit 3; saying so explicitly keeps "a gate with no entry
# is an error" intact, and catches the opposite drift too -- a gate that starts
# examining a fixture it was declared irrelevant to.

gradle-wrapper=n/a
jvm-test=n/a
# 10, calibrated from a FRESH CLONE rather than from a working copy.
#
# Set at 15 initially, from this host, where `git rev-list --all` reported 25.
# CI reported 13 and the floor failed. The gap was not the shallow clone -- that
# was a separate defect fixed in the same change -- it was six stale
# refs/remotes/origin/* entries for branches deleted on GitHub that a local
# fetch had never pruned. The floor had quietly encoded one developer's ref
# debris.
#
# A floor is a claim about what a gate should see. Calibrate it where the gate
# actually runs: `git clone` to a temp dir and measure there.
secrets=10
shellcheck=20
# 40, against 58 measured on a fresh clone of main. Raised from 20, which was
# calibrated when this repository's prose was one README. Moving the long form
# into docs/wiki/ and widening the gate's prose set took the denominator from 28
# to 58, and a floor of 20 against 58 cannot detect anything short of deleting
# most of the documentation -- which is the criticism this repository levels at
# other people's checks.
#
# Margin is deliberate. A floor at the observed value goes red on the next
# commit that legitimately removes a page, and a check that cries wolf gets
# deleted.
#
# WHAT 40 ACTUALLY CATCHES, measured on a fresh clone rather than reasoned:
#
#   58   baseline, passes
#   51   two wiki pages deleted -- ABOVE the floor, so the floor does not fire.
#        The gate still fails, on wiki-page-orphaned and dead-relative-link,
#        because the sidebar still points at them. A different control caught
#        it, and saying so here is the point: a floor that gets credit for a
#        catch it did not make is how the next person over-trusts it.
#   16   docs/wiki deleted entirely -- BELOW the floor, so this is the case the
#        floor exists for, and the one no link check could see, because links
#        to nothing removed are not broken.
#
# So the floor covers wholesale loss and section 7 covers partial loss. Neither
# covers a page that is quietly emptied of content while keeping its links
# intact; that would want a fault, and there is not one.
docs=40
